beats.content:
The top-level `styles` key in theme.json styles your theme at three levels:

- **Root (global):** properties directly under `styles`, such as `styles.color`, apply to the `<body>` and cascade down to everything.
- **Elements:** `styles.elements` targets things like links and buttons across every block.
- **Blocks:** `styles.blocks` targets one block type, using its full name, such as `core/code`.

```json
"styles": {
  "color": { "background": "#ffffff", "text": "#1e1e1e" },
  "elements": {
    "button": { "color": { "background": "#1e1e1e", "text": "#ffffff" } }
  },
  "blocks": {
    "core/code": { "color": { "background": "#f0f0f0" } }
  }
}
```

Styles set here show up in **Appearance > Editor > Styles**, so the people using your theme can change them without fighting CSS specificity. That's why the handbook recommends theme.json styles over a stylesheet wherever they can do the job.

The elements you can style include:

- `link` for `<a>` links
- `button` for buttons and button-like links, such as the Button block
- `heading` for all headings `<h1>` to `<h6>`, or `h1` through `h6` one at a time
- `caption` for media captions, and `cite` for citations in quotes

Links and buttons also accept pseudo-classes, nested under the element, including `:hover`, `:focus`, `:active` and `:visited`.

```json
"elements": {
  "link": {
    "color": { "text": "#3858e9" },
    ":hover": { "color": { "text": "#1e1e1e" } }
  }
}
```

If a block has its own style, it wins over the element style. For example, Button block styles override `elements.button`.

files.theme.json:
{
  "$schema": "https://schemas.wp.org/trunk/theme.json",
  "version": 3,
  "settings": {
    "useRootPaddingAwareAlignments": true,
    "color": {
      "palette": [
        { "name": "Base", "slug": "base", "color": "#ffffff" },
        { "name": "Contrast", "slug": "contrast", "color": "#1e1e1e" },
        { "name": "Subtle", "slug": "subtle", "color": "#f0f0f0" },
        { "name": "Accent", "slug": "accent", "color": "#3858e9" }
      ]
    },
    "layout": {
      "contentSize": "40rem",
      "wideSize": "64rem"
    },
    "typography": {
      "fontFamilies": [
        {
          "name": "System Sans",
          "slug": "system-sans",
          "fontFamily": "system-ui, -apple-system, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, sans-serif"
        }
      ]
    }
  },
  "styles": {
    "color": {
      "background": "var:preset|color|base",
      "text": "var:preset|color|contrast"
    },
    "spacing": {
      "padding": {
        "top": "0",
        "right": "1.5rem",
        "bottom": "0",
        "left": "1.5rem"
      }
    },
    "typography": {
      "fontFamily": "var:preset|font-family|system-sans",
      "lineHeight": "1.6"
    },
    "elements": {
      "link": {
        "color": { "text": "var:preset|color|accent" }
      },
      "heading": {
        "typography": { "fontWeight": "700", "lineHeight": "1.2" }
      }
    }
  },
  "templateParts": [
    { "name": "header", "title": "Header", "area": "header" },
    { "name": "footer", "title": "Footer", "area": "footer" }
  ]
}
